From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tangenx <me@tangenx.dev>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:30:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: dim the name and alias fields and allow deleting them

The dialogs used a bare android.widget.EditText, so the hint inherited
the plain black dialog text. They now use the stock EditTextBoldCursor
with a themed hint colour, and the alias field shows a dimmed @ as a
prefix instead of hinting '@alias', which read as part of the value.
Both dialogs get a Delete button when a value is already stored, and
storage accessors ignore the feature toggle so cleanup works with the
toggle off.

Constraint: fork strings stay in strings_tele.xml, stock labels are reused
Rejected: keeping '@alias' as the hint | it invites typing the @ that is not allowed
Confidence: high
Scope-risk: narrow
---
